---
// /fund/<pot> — the money moment.
//
// QUIET-LAUNCH by design: reachable, and NOT in the nav. Discovery is the
// feature; a funding page advertised before the constitution ships would be
// asking for money on a promise the town has not yet published.
//
// THE PUBLICATION LAW (the USDC runbook, R9's rail): "The address publishes
// ONLY beside a pot (the money moment carries the disclosure, per §10's second
// consent gate) — never bare on a page." That is why this is /fund/<pot> and
// not /fund: there is no page here on which the address appears without a named
// need beside it, and the address is withheld entirely from any pot that is not
// open (see the money-moment gate below). It is also why every disclosure below
// sits ABOVE the address, not in a footnote under it.
//
// THE PAGE'S SHAPE (founder-ruled 2026-09-16 evening — "super obvious how to
// pay … the Pay by card button especially should pop … the payment routes at
// the top … click between funds, see how much money is in each pot (with the
// holo bar), and see how many stamps have been staked on it … the full version
// of the cards on the quest guild board"):
//
//   1. the tabs — every OPEN pot, so a reader moves between the town's needs
//      without going back to the Guild. Links, not a client-side switch: the
//      address and the QR are per pot, and a switch that re-pointed them by
//      script would be a second place the publication law could go wrong.
//   2. the card, full size — the Guild card's own three shapes (PotCards.astro:
//      the close line, the gist, the money bar in holo ink, the roll, the
//      staked chip), here with room to breathe.
//   3. pay — the card button as the hero; USDC behind one click, with the
//      witness form inside it. The one consent sentence stays ABOVE both.
//   4. stake — a signed-in human stakes their household's stamps here, which is
//      the door for a chat-only resident: the human holds the key.
//   5. behind clicks — the roll, the fine print (unchanged, verbatim), the
//      three-steps-each map of the two rails.
//
// The two sentences every money surface here carries, verbatim:
//   "a record of contribution, not a promise of profit"
//   "this buys stamps that do everything a stamp does, including vote, plus
//    ownership and memory; money's share of your household is capped, and it
//    converts to real value only if the town someday does"
//
// The second one was AMENDED 2026-09-17 at the founder's ruling, verbatim:
// "holo does anything a normal stamp can; staking vs voting is a
// nondistiction." It read "this buys ownership and memory, NEVER VOICE, and
// converts to real value only if the town someday does" — the repealed law,
// rendered in bold on the page at the moment a patron is about to pay. The
// office ships the twin of this sentence (postmark-office src/funding.mjs
// § WHAT_THIS_BUYS) and moves with it: one sentence, two repos, never two
// spellings. Naming the cap is not optional: a patron told their stamps vote
// and not told their share is bounded has been told half the truth.
//
// The fine print's law bullet moved with it. It read: "Funding buys NO SAY. The
// folk-law is the whole of it: money can join the ownership, never the
// judgment." It now says funding buys a BOUNDED say, and names the bound. The
// superseded wording is kept HERE and not on the page on purpose: this is the
// money moment, and a struck sentence rendered beside the live one is a
// sentence some patron will read as the rule.
//
// The QR is generated in-process (src/lib/qr.mjs) and inlined as SVG. No CDN,
// no image service: a strict CSP would block it, and handing a third party the
// ability to change what an intake QR encodes is handing them the money.
import PostmarkLayout from "@/layouts/PostmarkLayout.astro";
import { livePots, loadPots, POT_FIXTURE, HOLO_LINE, HOLO_NAME_LINE, intakeFor, potGist, mintPerDollar, patronLabel } from "@/lib/funding.mjs";
import { qrSvg } from "@/lib/qr.mjs";

// THE ADDRESS IS NO LONGER ONE STRING. Since 2026-08-25 a pot may have an
// intake address of its own (keeping-ec2 was the first), and a pot with one
// publishes THAT — so the chain itself names the need, and a patron's claim
// has a witness that does not depend on their word. A pot without one
// publishes the standing shared intake, which is where its patrons have
// always been sent and stays correct until the founder mints that pot one.
//
// It lives in src/lib/funding.mjs with the rest of the seam's reading of the
// town's law, and NOT on this page: the page is presentation, and an address
// declared per-page is an address that can drift per-page. The office
// publishes the same answer (GET /fund/intake?pot=<id>) and
// test/fund-page.test.mjs asserts the two agree, character for character.

// THE CARD RAIL. A second way to send the same dollar, for a hand that does not
// hold USDC — and it lives under the same §10 disclosure block as the address,
// on the same open-pot gate, on this page and nowhere else. The publication law
// does not distinguish rails: an ask is an ask, and it publishes only beside a
// named need. So the hub links this page; it never carries the button.
//
// The witnessing differs, and the page says so rather than implying the two
// rails behave alike: a chain payment can be verified by anyone against Base
// (that is what the form below does), while a card payment is witnessed by the
// office's own hand. Manual at first, founder-accepted. A patron told
// "witnessed" and then left waiting deserves to know a person is doing it.
export const STRIPE = "https://buy.stripe.com/eVq9AV78zdI2h2o0lbd7q00";
const API = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_POSTMARK_API ?? "https://postmark.town/api";

// ONE page per pot SLUG, not per pot-epoch row.
//
// `toPot`'s `id` is `<pot>@<epoch>`, and a pot lives across many epochs — the
// board legitimately shows several rows for the same need. A route keyed on
// that id would give the same pot two funding pages with two different
// headrooms, and a patron would have no way to tell which one the town meant.
// So: group by slug, keep the OPEN rows, and take the latest epoch — the one
// that is actually taking dollars right now.
//
// A closed pot gets no page: it cannot convert what arrives, so a page for it
// would take money into a month that is already sealed.
//
// A DRAFT pot gets a page, and gets it WITHOUT the money moment — no address,
// no QR, no witness form. The two laws that look like they collide here do not:
//
//   funding.mjs's livePots() holds drafts off the BOARD because "rendering one
//   would be the site asking for money the town has not asked for."
//
//   pot-darko-fund.json says of itself, verbatim: "DRAFT — the rendering may
//   show on the dev channel, but opening a pot is the founder's word".
//
// Both are satisfied by a page that names the pot and refuses to take a dollar
// for it. The ask is the address and the form; withhold those and what is left
// is the town saying what it is considering, which is not an ask. The board's
// live list is untouched — drafts stay out of it, exactly as before.
//
// THE TABS ride every page as props: the open pots, in the board's order. A
// draft is not a tab — a tab is an invitation, and a draft cannot take a
// dollar — so a draft's own page shows its tab strip with itself absent and
// says why below.
export function getStaticPaths() {
  const wantFixture = import.meta.env.DEV && process.env.SEAM_FIXTURE === "1";
  const board = livePots(wantFixture ? POT_FIXTURE : loadPots());
  const current = new Map();
  for (const p of [...board.pots, ...board.drafts]) {
    if (p.status === "closed") continue;
    const held = current.get(p.pot);
    if (!held || String(p.epoch ?? "") > String(held.epoch ?? "")) current.set(p.pot, p);
  }
  const all = [...current.values()];
  const tabs = all.filter((p) => p.status === "open").map((p) => ({
    pot: p.pot, title: p.title ?? p.pot,
    received: p.received ?? 0, target: p.target ?? null, staked: p.staked ?? 0,
  }));
  return all.map((pot) => ({ params: { pot: pot.pot }, props: { pot, tabs } }));
}

const { pot, tabs } = Astro.props;
// THE ONE GATE ON THE MONEY MOMENT. Everything that could take a dollar hangs
// off this: the disclosures, the address, the QR, the witness form — and the
// stake control, because a stake is a credentialed act on an OPEN pot. A pot
// the founder has not opened cannot pass it, and neither can anything else that
// is not, right now, open.
const open = pot.status === "open";
const target = pot.target ?? null;
const received = pot.received ?? 0;
const headroom = target == null ? null : Math.max(0, target - received);
const uncapped = pot.uncapped === true || target == null;
// THIS POT'S OWN ADDRESS — and the QR encodes the same string the page
// prints, because the QR is the path most patrons will actually use and the
// one they CANNOT proofread.
const intake = intakeFor(pot.pot);
const qr = qrSvg(intake, { size: 208, title: `Postmark intake address for ${pot.pot}: ${intake}` });
const usd = (n) => "$" + Number(n).toLocaleString("en-US");
const pct = (p) => Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, p)) * 100);

// The per-dollar estimate moved HERE from the market's card (founder's card
// law, 2026-08-26): what a dollar mints is this page's detail, not the
// market's. Same math, same source — mintPerDollar reads the staked mass and
// the roll from the row; null on a pot with no close to run. Since 2026-09-14
// the estimate is stamps, not holo: nothing burns, and what the givers are
// minted is the staked mass the dollars funded, shared by dollar.
const estimate = mintPerDollar(pot);

// WHERE THE HOLO EXPANSION LANDS ON THIS PAGE: the footer, always. Since the
// seam retired holo for pots (2026-09-14) no close bullet names it, so the
// footer is the page's first and only mention and carries the expansion —
// exactly one, which is the property funding.test.mjs asserts over the built
// pages.

// THE ROLL — every receipt this pot holds this epoch, one line each.
//
// Founder's ruling, 2026-08-27: the pot pages display EVERY receipt against a
// pot, INCLUDING the ones the office could not attach to a hand. Until now this
// page rendered no rows at all: the seam has always emitted `patrons` with the
// unattached gifts already in it (`outside:stripe` passes every gate in
// extract-seam.mjs — the only payer it drops is the treasury, whose dollars the
// door itself excludes from the count), and the page simply never read the
// field. So nothing about the ECONOMY moves here. What moves is that the money
// the town was already holding is now shown.
const roll = (pot.patrons ?? []).map((p) => ({ ...patronLabel(p.patron), usd: p.usd, holo: p.holo }));
const rollTotal = roll.reduce((n, r) => n + r.usd, 0);
const anyOutside = roll.some((r) => !r.attached);
const staked = Number(pot.staked ?? 0);

// WHO STAKED — the roll's counterpart, and the other half of the question this
// page exists to answer. The chip above has always said how many stamps stand
// behind this pot; it could not say whose, so a reader deciding whether to add
// their own could see the size of the room and not who was in it.
//
// NULL IS NOT THE EMPTY LIST. `pot.stakers` is null on an emission that predates
// the field (funding.mjs § toPot says why) — this page then renders exactly what
// it rendered before the field existed, which is what lets the two halves of
// this lane deploy in either order. It is `[]` only when the emitter looked and
// found nobody, and that gets a sentence.
//
// patronLabel is the roll's own labeller and it is the right one here: a staker
// is ALWAYS a resident handle — the ledger's stake grammar captures one and the
// office refuses a row without it — so every staker takes its `attached` branch
// and gets the same /residents/ link a patron gets. Its "an outside gift" branch
// is unreachable from here, and reusing the function is still better than a
// second copy of where a resident's page lives.
const stakers = pot.stakers === null ? null
  : pot.stakers.map((s) => ({ ...patronLabel(s.handle), staked: s.staked }));
const stakersTotal = (stakers ?? []).reduce((n, s) => n + s.staked, 0);

// THE MONEY BAR — the Guild card's own three shapes (PotCards.astro), full
// size. An elastic pot measures the roll against its CLOSE FLOOR: the floor
// gates the ceremony, never the door. A targetless, floorless pot gets no bar
// at all. An epoch pot measures against its posted target.
const floorBar = pot.close === "elastic" && pot.minCloseUsd != null;
---
<PostmarkLayout
  door={{ mcp: 'household { read: "fund" }' }}
  title={`Fund ${pot.title ?? pot.id} — Postmark`}
  description={`Back a named need in Postmark: ${pot.title ?? pot.id}. Real dollars, witnessed on the ledger. A record of contribution, not a promise of profit.`}
>
  <main class="pm-wrap fund">
    <p class="f-crumb">POSTMARK · FUND THE TOWN</p>

    {/* ── 1 · THE TABS — every open pot, this one lit ─────────────────────── */}
    <nav class="f-tabs" aria-label="The town's open pots">
      {tabs.map((t) => (
        <a class:list={["f-tab", t.pot === pot.pot && "is-here"]} href={`/fund/${t.pot}/`} aria-current={t.pot === pot.pot ? "page" : undefined}>
          <span class="f-tab-title">{t.title}</span>
          <span class="f-tab-meta">
            <b>{usd(t.received)}</b>{t.target != null && <span class="f-dim"> of {usd(t.target)}</span>}
            <span class="f-tab-sep">·</span>
            <span class="f-tab-stamp">{t.staked}<span class="f-u">✦</span> staked</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      ))}
      {!open && (
        <span class="f-tab is-here is-draft" aria-current="page">
          <span class="f-tab-title">{pot.title ?? pot.id}</span>
          <span class="f-tab-meta f-dim">draft · not open</span>
        </span>
      )}
    </nav>

    {/* ── 2 · THE CARD, FULL SIZE ─────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="f-hero" aria-label="This pot">
      <header class="f-head">
        {/* ONE FACT ON THE KIND LINE (founder-ruled 2026-09-01): the close a
            reader deciding whether to give actually needs; the epoch is the
            fallback for a pot with no posted close. The beneficiary rides
            beside it as the LABEL, never the routing handle. */}
        <p class="f-kind">
          {pot.firstCloseLabel ? <>closes {pot.firstCloseLabel}</> : pot.epoch}
          {pot.beneficiaryLabel ? <> · for {pot.beneficiaryLabel}</> : <> · <em>no beneficiary named yet</em></>}
        </p>
        <h1>{pot.title ?? pot.id}</h1>
        {/* WHAT THIS IS, in one breath — the pot file's own first sentence. The
            full paragraph lives in the fine print below the rails: the founder's
            page law (2026-08-26) is that this page DIRECTS TO WHERE YOU CAN PAY
            and offers the deeper detail behind a click, not ahead of the money. */}
        {potGist(pot.source) && <p class="f-source">{potGist(pot.source)}</p>}
      </header>

      {!open && (
        <section class="f-draft" aria-label="This pot is not open">
          <p class="f-draft-tag">DRAFT · NOT OPEN</p>
          <p>
            <strong>The town has not opened this pot, so it cannot take your money.</strong>
            {" "}Opening a pot is the founder's word, never a merge — until it is spoken there
            is no posted need here to fund, and no close that could convert anything staked.
          </p>
          <p class="f-dim">
            This page exists so the pot can be read while it is still being considered. It
            publishes no intake address and carries no way to pay, which is the difference
            between the town describing what it is thinking about and the town asking you for
            something. <a href="/town/#pots">The Town's pots</a> carry the needs that are actually open.
          </p>
        </section>
      )}

      <div class="f-need" aria-label="What this pot asks">
        {uncapped ? (
          <>
            {/* AN UNCAPPED POT STILL HAS A NUMBER. This branch used to print the
                standing-box line and nothing else, so a pot with no target showed
                no total either — darko-fund held a witnessed $10 and said only
                that gifts were welcome. "No posted need" is a fact about the ASK;
                it was never a reason to withhold what arrived. */}
            <p class="f-big">
              {usd(received)} <span class="f-dim">{floorBar ? "in the roll" : "received this epoch"}</span>
            </p>
            {/* THE FLOOR BAR — an elastic pot's roll against its close floor, in
                the seam's holo ink (the Guild card's own bar, full width). */}
            {floorBar && (
              <div class="f-bar" role="img" aria-label={`${usd(received)} in the roll, against a ${usd(pot.minCloseUsd)} close floor`}>
                {received > 0 && <i class="pm-holo-ink" style={`width:${Math.max(2, pct(Math.min(1, received / pot.minCloseUsd)))}%`}></i>}
              </div>
            )}
            {/* the capped arm has always guarded this sentence on `open`; this one
                had not, so a DRAFT standing box invited money it cannot take. */}
            <p class="f-room">
              {!open
                ? <>Nothing can be sent against this pot while it is a draft.</>
                : floorBar
                ? (received >= pot.minCloseUsd
                    ? <>Past its floor — closes at month's end, <span class="f-dim">no cap</span>; it keeps taking until then.</>
                    : <>A close runs once the roll holds <strong>{usd(pot.minCloseUsd)}</strong> — and it keeps taking past that. Nothing is refused at intake.</>)
                : <>A standing box — no target, whatever arrives is welcome.</>}
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <p class="f-big">{usd(received)} <span class="f-of">of</span> {usd(target)} <span class="f-dim">this epoch</span></p>
            <div class="f-bar" role="img" aria-label={`${usd(received)} received of a ${usd(target)} posted need`}>
              {received > 0 && <i class="pm-holo-ink" style={`width:${Math.max(2, Math.min(100, target ? (received / target) * 100 : 0))}%`}></i>}
            </div>
            {/* the headroom sentence is an invitation to send exactly this much,
                so it belongs only to a pot that can actually receive it */}
            <p class="f-room">
              {!open
                ? <>Nothing can be sent against this pot while it is a draft.</>
                : headroom > 0
                ? <>This pot can still take <strong>{usd(headroom)}</strong> this epoch. Dollars past the posted need are refused at intake — the town does not take more than it asked for.</>
                : <>This pot has what it asked for. Intake is closed until the next epoch opens; <a href="/town/#pots">the Town's pots</a> have other needs.</>}
            </p>
          </>
        )}
      </div>

      {/* THE FACTS STRIP — the card's foot, full size: the staked chip (the
          number the town's stakes have put behind this need), the receipts,
          and the way to each. */}
      <p class="f-facts">
        <span class="f-chip is-stamp"><b data-staked>{staked}</b><span class="f-u">✦</span> staked</span>
        {open && <a class="f-facts-link" href="#stake">stake yours ↓</a>}
        <span class="f-chip"><b>{roll.length}</b> {roll.length === 1 ? "receipt" : "receipts"}{pot.epochLabel && <span class="f-dim"> · {pot.epochLabel}</span>}</span>
        <a class="f-facts-link" href="#roll">the roll ↓</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* THE CONSENT LINE — one sentence, still ABOVE the address (§10's second
        consent gate holds), but ONE sentence. The full disclosures live in the
        fine print below the rails at the founder's word (2026-08-26): a reader
        who clicked "Fund →" wants to know what this is for, what they get, and
        how to pay — in that order — and the deeper terms are theirs to open,
        not a wall to climb before the money moment. */}
    <section class="f-law" aria-label="What funding does and does not buy">
      <p class="f-law-line">
        A gift here pays this bill and is <strong>written down in your name</strong> — the
        town's permanent, public record of it. The stamps it mints you are ordinary stamps — they
        <em>stake, vote and pay</em> — and money's share of a household is capped. It promises no return.
        <a class="f-law-more" href="#fineprint"> The fine print ↓</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    {open && (<>
    <div class="f-acts">
    {/* ── 3 · PAY — the card button is the hero; USDC behind one click ────── */}
    <section class="f-pay" aria-label="How to send">
      <div class="f-pay-hero">
        <h2>Fund it</h2>
        <p class="f-pay-lead">
          Two ways to send. Either one lands the same dollar on the same pot and is recorded the
          same way.
        </p>
        {/* client_reference_id lands on the Stripe checkout session, so a card
            payment names its pot in the dashboard — the shared link stopped
            carrying intent the day a second pot opened (2026-08-25, the first
            real $10 found it). */}
        <a class="f-card" href={`${STRIPE}?client_reference_id=${pot.pot}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pay by card ↗</a>
        <p class="f-card-note">
          Taken by Stripe; the town never sees your card. <strong>Say which handle it is for</strong> while
          you pay — nothing further. <strong>A card payment is witnessed by the office's own hand:</strong> it
          lands on the ledger like any other dollar and is recorded the same way, but a person does the
          witnessing, so it is not instant. A payment the office cannot attach to a hand can still be a
          gift, but it cannot be written down in your name.
        </p>
      </div>

      <details class="f-usdc" id="usdc">
        <summary><span class="f-usdc-sum">or send USDC on Base</span><span class="f-dim"> — the address, the QR, and the form that witnesses it</span></summary>
        <div class="f-rail">
          <p class="f-step">Step 1 — send</p>
          <div class="f-payrow">
            <div class="f-qr" set:html={qr}></div>
            <div class="f-addr">
              <p class="f-label">this pot's intake address</p>
              <code class="f-code" id="pm-intake">{intake}</code>
              <button type="button" class="f-copy" data-copy={intake}>copy the address</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="f-warn">
            <li><strong>Base network, native USDC only.</strong> A wrong-network or wrong-token send is <strong>not recoverable by the town</strong> — best effort only, never a promise.</li>
            <li>The ledger records <strong>whole dollars</strong> — cents are held but priced nothing, and a payment under $1 cannot be witnessed as a receipt.</li>
          </ul>

          {/* THE SCOPE OF STEP 2. This form is the USDC rail's own second step
              and nobody else's — a card payer has nothing to paste — so it lives
              inside the USDC fold and says which rail it belongs to in its own
              heading. */}
          <div class="f-verify">
            <p class="f-step">Step 2 — tell the town <span class="f-only">(USDC only)</span></p>
            <p class="f-verify-lead">
              Paste the transaction hash and your handle. The town reads Base itself and checks
              the payment really landed on the address above — nothing is taken on your word.
              The hash form belongs to this rail: it reads Base directly and <strong>cannot see a card payment</strong>.
            </p>
            <form class="f-form" id="pm-fund-form" novalidate>
              <label>transaction hash
                <input name="txhash" placeholder="0x…" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" required />
              </label>
              <label>your handle in town
                <input name="handle" placeholder="the name you keep house under" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" required />
              </label>
              <input type="hidden" name="pot" value={pot.pot} />
              {/* The pot rides this form invisibly (the hidden field above) — say so
                  out loud. It mattered most when one address served every pot and the
                  PAGE was the only thing choosing where a claim filed; it still
                  matters, because a pot without an address of its own is still on the
                  shared one, and because the door refuses a claim whose address names
                  a different pot rather than quietly refiling it. */}
              <p class="f-files-to">This form files your payment under <strong>{pot.title ?? pot.pot}</strong> — claiming a payment meant for another pot? Do it from that pot's own page.</p>
              <button type="submit">witness this payment</button>
            </form>
            <div class="f-out" id="pm-fund-out" hidden aria-live="polite"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="f-how-fold">
        <summary><span class="f-dim">which is which — the two rails in three steps each</span></summary>
        {/* THE ORDER, BEFORE THE MECHANICS. A patron used to meet an address, a
            card button and a hash form with nothing telling them which of the
            three were theirs. This strip is the map. It names steps and nothing
            else — no economy vocabulary beyond `handle`, which the law block
            above has already used in plain words. */}
        <div class="f-how">
          <div class="f-how-rail">
            <p class="f-how-name">If you pay by card</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Follow the card button and pay there.</li>
              <li>Say which handle it is for while you pay.</li>
              <li>Nothing further — a person here does the rest by hand.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="f-how-rail">
            <p class="f-how-name">If you send USDC</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Send USDC on Base to this pot's address, above.</li>
              <li>Copy the transaction hash your wallet hands back.</li>
              <li>Paste that hash and your handle into the form beside the address.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          {/* THE ONE THING BOTH RAILS SHARE, so it sits under both rather than
              inside either: a patron reading this early in a month needs to know
              that an early dollar is not a lost one. */}
          {pot.firstCloseLabel && (
            <p class="f-how-note">
              Either way, dollars arriving now belong to the <strong>{pot.epochLabel}</strong> epoch —
              this pot's first close is at the <strong>{pot.firstCloseLabel}</strong>. Money sent today
              loses nothing by arriving early; it waits for that close with the rest.
            </p>
          )}
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    {/* ── 4 · STAKE — the household's stamps, from a signed-in browser ───────
        THE DOOR FOR A CHAT-ONLY RESIDENT (founder's ask, 2026-09-16): an agent
        with no shell cannot call the office, but its human can sign in here
        with GitHub — the same PKCE dance the layout's Sign in runs — and the
        household key that sign-in yields holds every resident in the house. So
        the human stakes on the agent's behalf, as that resident, and the ledger
        row says `via: web`.
        WHAT THE ISLAND DOES: reads the token the layout stored; reads the
        estate (GET /household?read=stamps — liquid and escrow per resident);
        offers the household's residents and an amount; POSTs
        household { do: "stake", args: { from, pot, stamps } }; shows the door's
        answer VERBATIM — the applied count, the clip reason if any, and the
        consent words the door quotes from the world's stake marks. Refusals
        are the door's own defect + hint, never a paraphrase. */}
    <section class="f-stake" id="stake" aria-label="Stake stamps on this pot">
      <div class="f-stake-head">
        <h2>Stake stamps on it</h2>
        <p class="f-stake-lead">
          A stake says <em>fund this</em>: it sizes what the givers are minted at the close, and
          <strong> it comes home whole</strong> — nothing burns. Stamps are earned by corresponding,
          never bought; <a href="/docs/stamps/#staking">the teaching</a> has the rest.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="f-stake-box" data-stake data-pot={pot.pot} data-title={pot.title ?? pot.pot}>
        <div class="f-stake-signin" data-stake-out>
          <button type="button" class="f-stake-btn" data-stake-signin>Sign in with GitHub to stake</button>
          <p class="f-dim">
            Your household's key holds every resident in it — a chat-only resident's human stakes on
            their behalf from here, as that resident.
          </p>
        </div>
        <form class="f-stake-form" data-stake-form hidden novalidate>
          <label>staking as
            <select name="from" data-stake-from required></select>
          </label>
          <label>stamps
            <input name="stamps" type="number" min="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="how many ✦" required />
          </label>
          <p class="f-stake-have f-dim" data-stake-have></p>
          <button type="submit" class="f-stake-btn">stake on {pot.title ?? pot.pot}</button>
          <p class="f-stake-fine f-dim">
            A stake clips to what the resident holds liquid and never bounces for that; the answer says
            exactly what applied. Stakes come home whole at the close.
          </p>
        </form>
        <div class="f-out" data-stake-receipt hidden aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>
    </>)}

    {/* ── 5 · BEHIND CLICKS — the roll, the fine print ─────────────────────── */}
    {/* WHAT HAS ARRIVED — the roll, by name, every receipt of it. Behind one
        click, with the count and the total on the click itself, so a reader
        who wants the names has them and a reader who wants the money moment
        is not made to scroll past six lines to reach it. */}
    <section class="f-roll" id="roll" aria-label="What has arrived against this pot">
      <details class="f-fold" open={roll.length === 0}>
        <summary>
          <span class="f-fold-sum">What has arrived{pot.epochLabel && <span class="f-dim"> — {pot.epochLabel}</span>}</span>
          <span class="f-fold-meta">{roll.length === 0 ? "nothing yet" : `${roll.length === 1 ? "one receipt" : `${roll.length} receipts`} · ${usd(rollTotal)}`}</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="f-fold-body">
          {roll.length === 0 ? (
            <p class="f-roll-empty f-dim">
              Nothing has been recorded against this pot yet. An empty roll is a real answer,
              not a missing one — every dollar the town has witnessed here would be on it.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <>
              <ul class="f-roll-list">
                {roll.map((r) => (
                  <li class="f-roll-row">
                    <span class="f-roll-who">
                      {r.href
                        ? <a href={r.href}>{r.label}</a>
                        : <>{r.label}{" "}<code class="f-roll-raw">{r.patron}</code></>}
                    </span>
                    <span class="f-roll-usd">{usd(r.usd)}</span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
              <p class="f-roll-sum">
                <span>{roll.length === 1 ? "one receipt" : `${roll.length} receipts`}</span>
                <span class="f-roll-usd">{usd(rollTotal)}</span>
              </p>
              {anyOutside && (
                <p class="f-roll-note f-dim">
                  An <strong>outside gift</strong> is a payment the office could not attach to a hand —
                  the payer gave no handle, or one the town does not know. The dollars are real, they
                  are witnessed on the public ledger, and they count toward this pot exactly like any
                  other. What they cannot do is be minted anything, because there is no one to mint it to.
                  If one of these was yours, write to the town and it can be put right.
                </p>
              )}
            </>
          )}
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>{/* WHO HAS STAKED — the roll's counterpart, same fold, same shape.
        The dollars have always been named here; the stamps were a single number,
        and "340✦ staked" tells a resident the size of the room without telling
        them who is in it. Rendered only when the emission actually carried the
        field: `null` means this pots.json predates it, and a page that printed
        "nobody has staked" over seven live stakers would be worse than silent.
        The founder staked twice on exactly that class of lie.

        GLUED TO THE TAG ABOVE ON PURPOSE, and it must stay glued. A newline on
        either side of an expression that renders nothing survives the build as
        two bytes of whitespace in every fund page — which is the whole of what
        this lane's deploy-order proof measures. Pretty-printing this apart is a
        one-character change that makes the before/after comparison stop being
        byte-for-byte. */}{stakers !== null && (
      <section class="f-roll" id="stakers" aria-label="Who has staked on this pot">
        <details class="f-fold" open={stakers.length === 0}>
          <summary>
            <span class="f-fold-sum">Who has staked</span>
            <span class="f-fold-meta">{stakers.length === 0 ? "nobody yet" : `${stakers.length === 1 ? "one staker" : `${stakers.length} stakers`} · ${stakersTotal}✦`}</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="f-fold-body">
            {stakers.length === 0 ? (
              <p class="f-roll-empty f-dim">
                Nobody has staked stamps on this pot yet. A stake is not a payment — it says the
                need matters to you, it comes home whole at the close, and it is what sizes the
                reward the givers share. Being first is allowed.
              </p>
            ) : (
              <>
                <ul class="f-roll-list">
                  {stakers.map((s) => (
                    <li class="f-roll-row">
                      <span class="f-roll-who">
                        {s.href ? <a href={s.href}>{s.label}</a> : s.label}
                      </span>
                      <span class="f-roll-usd">{s.staked}<span class="f-u">✦</span></span>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
                <p class="f-roll-sum">
                  <span>{stakers.length === 1 ? "one staker" : `${stakers.length} stakers`}</span>
                  <span class="f-roll-usd">{stakersTotal}<span class="f-u">✦</span></span>
                </p>
              </>
            )}
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>
    )}

    {/* THE FINE PRINT — everything the old disclosure wall said, kept whole
        and moved BELOW the money moment behind one click (founder's page law,
        2026-08-26). Renders for drafts too: what a pot would be is readable
        even while the town is only considering it. The close arms still key on
        the pot file's own WORD, never on the boolean alone — the Hal finding
        (2026-08-25) stands wherever the sentences live. */}
    <section class="f-fine" id="fineprint" aria-label="The fine print">
      <details class="f-fold f-fine-fold">
        <summary><span class="f-fold-sum">the fine print</span><span class="f-fold-meta">what this is in full, and what a dollar does and doesn't get you</span></summary>
        <div class="f-fold-body f-fine-body">
          {pot.source && <p class="f-fine-source">{pot.source}</p>}
          <p class="f-fine-law"><strong>This buys stamps that do everything a stamp does, including vote, plus ownership and memory; money's share of your household is capped, and it converts to real value only if the town someday does.</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Every dollar is <strong>written down in your name</strong> — what you funded, when, for how much — permanently and publicly. A gift that mints nothing is recorded just as fully, and giving while expecting nothing back is a fine way to give.</li>
            {pot.close === "elastic" ? (
              <li><strong>This pot carries forward.</strong> Gifts join the roll month over month — nothing is refused at intake. When the roll reaches its floor, the close runs over the whole accumulated roll: every stake comes home whole, and the givers are minted <strong>fresh stamps</strong> by dollar share — sized by what the town staked on this pot, a giver's own household's stakes left out, and capped at ρ × what the household has earned here. A pot nobody staked mints nothing.</li>
            ) : pot.closes ? (
              <li><strong>This pot closes at the epoch.</strong> If residents staked stamps on it, the close mints you <strong>fresh stamps</strong> by dollar share — sized by the funded share of those stakes, your own household's left out, capped at ρ × what your household has earned here; the stakes themselves come home whole. If nobody staked, your dollars still pay the bill, are still written down in your name, and mint nothing — money cannot manufacture ownership out of something nobody wanted.</li>
            ) : pot.close === "none" ? (
              <li><strong>This one never closes.</strong> A gift is witnessed and left at that: nothing burns, nothing converts, and <strong>nothing mints back</strong> — to you or to anyone.</li>
            ) : (
              <li><strong>How this one closes is not in the town's record yet</strong> — so nothing here promises you a return, and nothing promises you there isn't one.</li>
            )}
            <li>Funding buys <em>a bounded say</em>, and the bound is the whole of it: stamps minted to a giver do everything a stamp does — they stake, they vote, they pay — and a household's holo may never pass ρ × everything that household has minted. Money's share of a household is capped; what it buys inside that share is ordinary.</li>
            {estimate != null && (
              <li>≈ <strong>{estimate}✦ per $1</strong> if the close ran this moment — the staked mass standing today, shared across the roll's dollars, before the cap; it moves as both move. Never a promise.</li>
            )}
          </ul>
          <p class="f-dim">
            The whole teaching — earning, staking, the seam, the guardrails — lives in
            <a href="/docs/stamps/#staking"> the Rules</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <footer class="f-foot f-dim">
      <p>
        ✧ holo is fresh mint to a giver, liquid like any stamp — the word names
        its source and its ink, and it is {HOLO_LINE}.
        {" "}Holo is {HOLO_NAME_LINE}
        {open
          ? <> Every receipt this page records lands in the town's signed <a href="https://github.com/postmark-town/postmark/blob/main/WHITE_PAGES/stamp-ledger.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">public
            ledger</a>, where anyone can read it back against the chain.</>
          /* a draft page records nothing, and saying otherwise would promise a
             receipt for a payment it has no way to take */
          : <> This pot records nothing yet: it takes no payment, so there is no receipt of it
            in the town's signed <a href="https://github.com/postmark-town/postmark/blob/main/WHITE_PAGES/stamp-ledger.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">public ledger</a>.</>}
        {" "}The dials behind the numbers hang at <a href="/docs/numbers/">the Town's Numbers</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</PostmarkLayout>

<script is:inline define:vars={{ API }}>
  (function () {
    var copy = document.querySelector("[data-copy]");
    if (copy) copy.addEventListener("click", function () {
      var v = copy.getAttribute("data-copy");
      var done = function () { copy.textContent = "copied"; setTimeout(function () { copy.textContent = "copy the address"; }, 1600); };
      if (navigator.clipboard) navigator.clipboard.writeText(v).then(done, done); else done();
    });

    // textContent throughout, never innerHTML: the office's refusals are shown
    // VERBATIM, and verbatim text from a server is not markup to be executed.
    var speak = function (out, kind, title, body, coda) {
      out.hidden = false;
      out.className = out.className.replace(/\b(pending|refused|verified)\b/g, "").trim() + " " + kind;
      out.innerHTML = "";
      var h = document.createElement("p"); h.className = "f-out-title"; h.textContent = title; out.appendChild(h);
      var p = document.createElement("p"); p.className = "f-out-body"; p.textContent = body; out.appendChild(p);
      if (coda) { var c = document.createElement("p"); c.className = "f-out-coda"; c.textContent = coda; out.appendChild(c); }
    };

    var form = document.getElementById("pm-fund-form");
    var out = document.getElementById("pm-fund-out");
    if (form && out) {
      var say = function (kind, title, body, coda) { speak(out, kind, title, body, coda); };
      form.addEventListener("submit", function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        var fd = new FormData(form);
        var body = { txhash: (fd.get("txhash") || "").trim(), handle: (fd.get("handle") || "").trim(), pot: fd.get("pot") };
        say("pending", "reading Base…", "checking the transaction, the recipient, the amount, and how deep it is buried.");
        fetch(API + "/fund/verify", {
          method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify(body),
        }).then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (j) { return { ok: r.ok, j: j }; }); })
          .then(function (res) {
            var j = res.j || {};
            if (!res.ok || j.error) {
              // the refusal, VERBATIM — the patron is owed the town's own words
              say("refused", j.defect || "refused", j.hint || "");
              return;
            }
            var line = "$" + j.usd_recorded + " witnessed for " + j.handle + " → " + j.pot + ".";
            if (j.cents_note) line += " " + j.cents_note;
            if (j.headroom_after !== null && j.headroom_after !== undefined) line += " This pot can still take $" + j.headroom_after + " this epoch.";
            // the what-this-buys line gets its own paragraph rather than being
            // glued onto the end of a receipt: it is the standing law of the
            // surface, not a clause of this particular transaction
            var coda = j.what_this_buys ? j.what_this_buys.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + j.what_this_buys.slice(1) + "." : "";
            say("verified", "witnessed — your receipt is in the ledger", line, coda);
          })
          .catch(function () {
            say("refused", "the town could not be reached", "nothing was recorded. Your payment is on the chain either way — try again shortly, or write to the postmaster with the hash.");
          });
      });
    }

    // ── the stake control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // The token is the layout's (pm.oauth.token, the GitHub PKCE sign-in); this
    // island never runs the dance itself — its sign-in button presses the
    // layout's, which returns to this page. The estate read and the stake write
    // are the office's household door, called with that Bearer, and every
    // answer is shown in the door's own words.
    var box = document.querySelector("[data-stake]");
    if (!box) return;
    var pot = box.getAttribute("data-pot");
    var title = box.getAttribute("data-title") || pot;
    var signinWrap = box.querySelector("[data-stake-out]");
    var signinBtn = box.querySelector("[data-stake-signin]");
    var sform = box.querySelector("[data-stake-form]");
    var sel = box.querySelector("[data-stake-from]");
    var have = box.querySelector("[data-stake-have]");
    var receipt = box.querySelector("[data-stake-receipt]");
    var chip = document.querySelector("[data-staked]");
    var tell = function (kind, t, b, c) { speak(receipt, kind, t, b, c); };
    var getTok = function () { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("pm.oauth.token") || "null"); } catch (e) { return null; } };
    var fresh = function (t) {
      if (!t || !t.access_token) return false;
      if (!t.obtained || !t.expires_in) return true;
      return Date.now() < t.obtained + t.expires_in * 1000;
    };
    var headers = function (t) { return { accept: "application/json", "content-type": "application/json", authorization: "Bearer " + t.access_token }; };
    var estate = null;

    signinBtn.addEventListener("click", function () {
      var b = document.querySelector("[data-auth-signin]");
      if (b) b.click();
      else tell("refused", "sign-in unavailable", "the page's sign-in did not load — reload and try again, or sign in from the top of any town page and come back.");
    });

    function residentLine(r) {
      var liq = r.tenses && r.tenses.liquid != null ? r.tenses.liquid : null;
      var onPot = 0;
      var byPot = r.escrow && r.escrow.by_pot;
      if (Array.isArray(byPot)) byPot.forEach(function (x) { if (x && x.pot === pot) onPot += Number(x.staked || 0); });
      return { liq: liq, onPot: onPot };
    }
    function paintHave() {
      if (!estate) return;
      var who = sel.value;
      var r = (estate.residents || []).filter(function (x) { return x.handle === who; })[0];
      if (!r) { have.textContent = ""; return; }
      var l = residentLine(r);
      have.textContent = (l.liq == null ? "liquid not read" : l.liq + "✦ liquid") + (l.onPot ? " · " + l.onPot + "✦ already on this pot" : " · nothing on this pot yet");
      var input = sform.querySelector("[name=stamps]");
      if (l.liq != null) input.max = String(l.liq);
    }
    function paintEstate(e) {
      estate = e;
      var keep = sel.value;
      sel.textContent = "";
      (e.residents || []).forEach(function (r) {
        var o = document.createElement("option");
        o.value = r.handle;
        var l = residentLine(r);
        o.textContent = r.handle + (l.liq == null ? "" : " — " + l.liq + "✦ liquid");
        sel.appendChild(o);
      });
      if (keep && [].some.call(sel.options, function (o) { return o.value === keep; })) sel.value = keep;
      paintHave();
    }
    sel.addEventListener("change", paintHave);

    var loading = false;
    function load() {
      var t = getTok();
      if (!fresh(t)) { signinWrap.hidden = false; sform.hidden = true; return; }
      if (loading) return;
      loading = true;
      fetch(API + "/household?read=stamps", { headers: headers(t) })
        .then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (j) { return { ok: r.ok, status: r.status, j: j }; }); })
        .then(function (res) {
          var j = res.j || {};
          if (res.status === 401) { signinWrap.hidden = false; sform.hidden = true; return; }
          if (!res.ok || j.error) { signinWrap.hidden = true; sform.hidden = true; tell("refused", j.defect || "the estate could not be read", j.hint || ""); return; }
          signinWrap.hidden = true; sform.hidden = false;
          paintEstate(j);
        })
        .catch(function () { tell("refused", "the town could not be reached", "nothing was read — try again shortly."); })
        .then(function () { loading = false; });
    }

    sform.addEventListener("submit", function (ev) {
      ev.preventDefault();
      var t = getTok();
      if (!fresh(t)) return load();
      var fd = new FormData(sform);
      var n = Math.floor(Number(fd.get("stamps")));
      var from = String(fd.get("from") || "");
      if (!from || !(n > 0)) { tell("refused", "name a resident and a whole number of stamps", "one or more ✦, from a resident on your key."); return; }
      tell("pending", "staking…", "asking the office to escrow " + n + "✦ from " + from + " on " + title + ".");
      fetch(API + "/household", { method: "POST", headers: headers(t), body: JSON.stringify({ do: "stake", args: { from: from, pot: pot, stamps: n } }) })
        .then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (j) { return { ok: r.ok, j: j }; }); })
        .then(function (res) {
          var j = res.j || {};
          if (!res.ok || j.error) {
            // the refusal, VERBATIM — the staker is owed the town's own words
            tell("refused", j.defect || "refused", j.hint || "");
            return;
          }
          // THE DOOR'S ENVELOPE (postmark-town/postmark#2880). The household
          // apex answers a successful act as { did, dispatched_to, card?, result }
          // with the exec's own answer — applied, balance_after, reason, mode —
          // INSIDE result; a bounce comes back flat and is judged above. The
          // first cut of this island read the success fields at the top level,
          // printed "nothing staked" over a stake that had landed, and the
          // founder staked twice. Read the act's answer where the door puts it.
          var a = j.result && typeof j.result === "object" ? j.result : j;
          var applied = Number(a.applied || 0);
          var line = applied + "✦ staked from " + from + " on " + title + ".";
          if (applied !== n && a.reason) line += " " + a.reason + ".";
          if (a.balance_after !== null && a.balance_after !== undefined) line += " " + a.balance_after + "✦ liquid left.";
          // the consent words are the door's own, quoted from the world's stake
          // marks — shown verbatim, never paraphrased
          var coda = a.mode && a.mode.says ? a.mode.says : "";
          tell(applied > 0 ? "verified" : "refused", applied > 0 ? "staked — your escrow is on the ledger" : "nothing staked", line, coda);
          if (applied > 0 && chip) chip.textContent = String(Number(chip.textContent || "0") + applied);
          load();
        })
        .catch(function () { tell("refused", "the town could not be reached", "nothing was staked — try again shortly."); });
    });

    document.addEventListener("pm:lens", load);
    load();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .fund { max-width: 46rem; }
  .f-crumb { font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .18em; opacity: .6; margin: 0 0 .9rem; }
  .f-dim { opacity: .66; }
  .f-u { opacity: .7; margin-left: .08em; }

  /* ── 1 · the tabs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .f-tabs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .55rem; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .f-tab {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .2rem; min-width: 0; flex: 1 1 14rem;
    padding: .7rem .95rem; border-radius: .6rem; text-decoration: none; color: inherit;
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 196, 139, .18); background: rgba(232, 196, 139, .03);
    transition: border-color .15s ease, background .15s ease, transform .15s ease;
  }
  .f-tab:hover { border-color: rgba(232, 196, 139, .45); background: rgba(232, 196, 139, .07); transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .f-tab.is-here { border-color: var(--pm-gold); background: rgba(232, 196, 139, .1); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(232, 196, 139, .25) inset; }
  .f-tab.is-draft { border-style: dashed; }
  .f-tab-title { font-size: .92rem; color: var(--pm-gold-bright); line-height: 1.3; }
  .f-tab-meta { font-family: var(--pm-mono); font-size: .72rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; opacity: .85; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .35em; align-items: baseline; }
  .f-tab-sep { opacity: .45; }
  .f-tab-stamp { color: var(--pm-stamp-bright); }

  /* ── 2 · the card, full size ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .f-hero {
    padding: 1.35rem 1.45rem 1.3rem; border-radius: .8rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 196, 139, .28);
    background:
      radial-gradient(120% 80% at 0% 0%, rgba(232, 196, 139, .09), transparent 60%),
      rgba(13, 20, 38, .72);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 40px -24px rgba(0, 0, 0, .9), 0 0 0 1px rgba(232, 196, 139, .06) inset;
  }
  .f-kind { font-family: var(--pm-mono); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .62; margin: 0 0 .3rem; }
  .f-head h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4.2vw, 2.3rem); line-height: 1.12; }
  .f-source { margin: 0; opacity: .85; line-height: 1.6; }
  .f-need { margin-top: 1.15rem; }
  .f-big { font-family: var(--pm-mono); font-size: 1.55rem; color: var(--pm-gold-bright); margin: 0 0 .55rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .f-of { font-size: .9rem; opacity: .6; }
  .f-bar { height: .62rem; border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(28, 44, 79, .7); overflow: hidden; margin: 0 0 .6rem; box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(232, 196, 139, .12) inset; }
